    "parse_ok": true,
    "reply": "Hello,\n\nThank you for raising this, and I'm sorry for the confusion the mismatched reading periods have caused. You're right to want the periods reconciled before any statement says the new price applies to all units.\n\nAn internal billing verification request has been created and is pending. It covers reconciling the meter reading intervals with the tariff change date so the units are allocated to the correct price period. Please note this is pending only; no review result or outcome is available yet.\n\nTo help the check identify your account, please reply with your account or customer reference number (not a password or PIN). If you can, also note the reading dates shown on the statement and the tariff change date as they appear there — that will let the periods be compared directly.\n\nUntil the reconciliation is confirmed, please treat the \"all units at the new price\" wording as unconfirmed rather than final. If you'd like an update on the pending request, just reply to this email.\n\nKind regards,\nCustomer Service",
